t many subjects were moving around to determine their heading direction according to the real-time updated tracker marker on the 3D mini map. Finally, for the global condition, few subjects made mistakes while navigating towards the target. It was observed that the subjects often performed a “Planning while comprehending” behavior while using egocentric AR cues. The process of understanding spatial information came naturally when they were heading towards the target while they could clearly tell the correlation of intersected hallways and obstacles while changing their perspective to avoid occlusion. This results in the least PAO result among 4 conditions, while being the most stable and consistent cueing method.

